            </profile>
            <profile id="ba9a-445d-ea38-5406" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">Hand weapon, thrusting spear and light armour. May have javelins (+1 pt), shield (+1 pt) and heavy armour instead of light armour (+1 pt). May exchange thrusting spear for double-handed axe (+2 pts), or a Dane Axe (+2 pts) that counts as a halberd. May be Riding Horses (+1 pt). Stubborn. Fearsome. May form a shieldwall or Svinfylking formation. The Varangoi count as Tagmata troops. Not available to Isaurian &amp; Phrygian armies. (Byzantium p.69)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="a08b-74d6-ab6b-a563" name="Armour Save" hidden="false" typeId="0dbe-f4ed-ef08-8e86" typeName="Armour Save">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Save" typeId="603e-2898-6af9-6cf1">6+</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="With conditional bonuses" typeId="5882-dd5a-bc28-4024">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Notes" typeId="d5e4-804e-6192-0114">Armour save from armour, shield and barding bonus pips (rulebook pp.95-98); maximum 3+ (2+ for barded cavalry). M already includes encumbrance for armour/barding (p.96). Conditional pips are in the next column.</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
