        <selectionEntry id="8527-c478-6104-d319" name="Syphon" hidden="false" collective="false" import="true" type="model">
          <constraints>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="dfd1-66a5-8bf8-b010" type="min"/>
            <constraint field="selections" scope="parent" value="1" percentValue="false" shared="false" includeChildSelections="false" includeChildForces="false" id="3799-cf79-48ab-133d" type="max"/>
          </constraints>
          <profiles>
            <profile id="94fb-450b-87cb-e45c" name="Syphon" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="a802-40b5-d980-cabc" typeName="Model">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="M" typeId="35a2-714d-db3e-3738">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="WS" typeId="bb04-2b70-ae79-3559">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="BS" typeId="ffff-54f0-d131-b6a9">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="S" typeId="9e7c-6fc0-c50c-ee53">5</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="T" typeId="d226-f704-80f9-6e23">6</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="W" typeId="ce59-af10-7f37-4238">2</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="I" typeId="8ec4-e9a6-0b8a-08aa">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="A" typeId="ee87-e286-4768-82be">-</characteristic>
                <characteristic name="Ld" typeId="b6d1-0987-3a4d-d6a9">-</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
            <profile id="3f18-9bda-1f99-1040" name="Equipment and options (as printed in WAB2 army list)" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false" typeId="b19e-ee0c-17d1-6e33" typeName="Equipment and Notes">
              <characteristics>
                <characteristic name="Text" typeId="63ac-8f60-d28a-2232">The Syphon may have two to four crewmen with a hand weapon, light armour and shield (8 pts each). Deployment: must be deployed as the last unit and in base contact with the Byzantine player's table edge. Cannot march or charge, and cannot move and shoot in the same turn. Shooting at the Syphon: counts as a war machine - all rules on pages 64-65 in the WAB rulebook apply; it does not count as a large target. Discharging Greek Fire: treated in the same way as javelins (range 8", no long range modifier) with a Strength of 5, causing D3 wounds in each model hit; armour saves are not allowed. Uses: the Syphon may be used a total of D6+2 times during each battle. In each Shooting phase, it may be discharged a number of times equal to the number of crewmen at the time of the discharge. As soon as the Greek Fire causes its first wound, the syphoneers cause terror. A unit that receives a wound from Greek Fire must take an immediate Panic test; if it panics it flees an extra D6". Count as Tagmata troops. 0-2 units. The author suggests getting your opponent's approval before fielding Greek Fire Syphoneers. (Byzantium p.70)</characteristic>
              </characteristics>
            </profile>
          </profiles>
          <costs>
            <cost name="pts" typeId="points" value="40"/>
          </costs>
        </selectionEntry>
