  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="0687-5de4-0338-b732" name="Thematic Byzantines (Byzantium) - List Notes" publicationId="15ea-5299-d0f5-5dbb" hidden="false">
      <description>THEMATIC BYZANTINES (Byzantium: Beyond the Golden Gate, pp.63-70): the themata and tagmata armies of the Isaurian, Phrygian and Macedonian Dynasties, c.660-1042 AD. The army is fielded either as a Themata army (themata troops only, led by a Strategos with a Themata Army Standard Bearer) or a Tagmata army (themata and tagmata troops, led by a Domestikos or the Emperor with an Imperial Army Standard); this is not enforced in the data - Tagmata-grade units are the ones named Tagmata, plus Varangoi Guards, Kataphraktoi and Greek Fire Syphons.

ARMY COMPOSITIONS (pick one in the Army composition list):
[Thematic Byzantines - Isaurian &amp; Phrygian Dynasties]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 66%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  ISAURIAN &amp; PHRYGIAN DYNASTIES (c.660-867 AD). Characters up to 25%; Infantry up to 66% (up to two units of Elite Themata Kontaratoi); Cavalry at least 25% (Kataphraktoi may not be chosen); Special Units up to 25% (Varangoi Guards may not be chosen); Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 25% on Early Slavs and Early Bulgars (no Brigands, no Balkan Ruse), Early Khazars and Alans (documented only). Special rules: armies led by a Domestikos or the Emperor may use the Stratagem special rule. Any unit of Themata or Elite Themata Kavallarioi, and any character leading them, may be upgraded to Akritai Border Cavalry (+1 pt; no Hippo-toxotai; Feigned Flight). Horse archery was in decline: all cavalry and infantry units with BS4 on their stat line that take bows count as having BS3 (-1 pt; not enforced). The army is either a Themata army (Themata troops and characters, Themata Army Standard Bearer, led by a Strategos) or a Tagmata army (Themata and Tagmata troops, Tagmata Army Standard Bearer, led by a Domestikos or the Emperor) - not enforced.
[Thematic Byzantines - Macedonian Dynasty]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: up to 50%
  Cavalry: at least 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  MACEDONIAN DYNASTY (867-1042 AD). Characters up to 25%; Infantry up to 50%; Cavalry at least 25%; Special Units up to 25%; Allies &amp; Mercenaries up to 25% on troops from the Era of the Princes Rus army, Later Khazars, Pechenegs and Alans (documented only). Special rules: Macedonian Dynasty armies led by a Domestikos, Emperor or Strategos may use the Stratagem special rule. One unit of Light Kavallarioi may be upgraded to Prokousatores (+1 pt; no more than 25% of the models may take bows instead of spears; Feigned Flight). For each Kontaratoi unit in the army, one unit of Psiloi (Elite Themata or Themata only) of up to ten models may be upgraded to Menaulatoi (+2 pts, +1 Ld, Light Infantry). The army is either a Themata army or a Tagmata army (see Isaurian &amp; Phrygian) - not enforced.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
